   Some of these are features, not bugs.  Your Master Lich could have
been a chameleon, since they can be any creature - even a genocided
type.  If the game is built with HARD #defined, wands of wishing have
1-3 charges when found, which is rude, but not a bug.

   As for choking, I'm *very* careful about it, and rarely choke.  The
version of hack I've logged the most hours on had no warning at all,
and you could choke while eating a wraith, so I'm grateful for the
warnings I get.  There may be a bug there, but it's fairly minor.
Once I had an amulet of life saving, and answered n to the stop
eating? prompt.  I choked, died, came back to life, and then died
again, which didn't seem right.

    Closing your eyes?  Sensible, but I guess it makes things too
easy.  What's the point of all those neat sounds if a player with
only telepathy can always know what's on the level.

- Bob

P.S.  My thanks to the dev team for a wonderful game (both PC and
unix). 


